---
title: Asian Vegetable Stock
description: This rich Asian vegetable stock is tasty enough to be sipped alone or used as a base for countless soups and noodle soups. It's truly a cornerstone recipe.
image: https://thewoksoflife.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/08/asian-vegetable-stock-8.jpg
prep time: 15 minutes
cuisine: Asian
course: Soups and Stocks
servings: 4
tags: vegetable stock
source: https://thewoksoflife.com/asian-vegetable-stock
time required: 5 hours 15 minutes
cook time: 5 hours
---

Preheat oven to 375 degrees F. Take your @napa cabbage{1/2}(cut in half lengthwise) and cut it in half again lengthwise. Place the cabbage on a #sheet pan{} and drizzle lightly with @vegetable oil{2%tablespoons}(divided). Roast for ~{25%minutes}.

Meanwhile, in a large #stockpot{}, heat @vegetable oil{1%tablespoon} over medium heat. Add @ginger{7% slices}(about 20g or 0.7 oz.) and @garlic{2%cloves}(peeled and cut in half) and cook for ~{2%minutes}, until fragrant but not browned. Add @?fermented bean curd{2%cubes}(about 0.8 ounces or 23g, optional) and cook for another minute. Then add @onion{1}(peeled and quartered), @carrots{1%pound}(450g, peeled and cut into large chunks), @scallions{8}(ends removed), @daikon radish{8 ounces}(225g, peeled and cut into chunks), @kombu{1}(5x5 inch piece dried kelp, rinsed), and @shiitake mushrooms{16}(dried, rinsed), along with @water{16 cups}(about 1 gallon or about 4L). When the napa cabbage is done roasting, add it to the pot as well.

Bring to a boil, turn the heat down to low, and simmer with the lid on for ~{240%minutes}.

Strain the stock, and season with @salt{to taste}.
